Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:19:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 135/136] Window Maker's root mouse actions and ViKeyMenus
 (WPrefs parity)

- RootMouse (Config.plist): each button opens the applications menu or
  nothing, the wheel and tilt switch workspaces or windows (up = next, as
  Button4), DisableActions turns them off. Read live: SIGHUP applies them.
- A menu opened by another button acts as with the right one: held, the
  release over an item runs it; clicked, it stays open, without the X.
- toolkit: root unclaimed_axis_event; wlmtk_menu_set_open_button;
  wlmtk_menu_set_vi_keys (h j k l as arrows, Config ViKeyMenus).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
